📦 Business Plan for The Pack Out King

1. Executive Summary
Business Name: The Pack Out KingLocation: Mesa, AZIndustry: Pack Out, Storage, Restoration SupportBusiness Model: B2B and B2C (insurance carriers, restoration companies, homeowners)
Overview:The Pack Out King is a professional contents handling company that specializes in packing out, storing, and packing back personal property from homes affected by disasters such as water, or mold damage. We work directly with insurance carriers, restoration contractors, and homeowners to provide fast, secure, and documented pack out services, ensuring seamless restoration workflows and peace of mind.

Mission Statement:To protect, document, and restore our customers' belongings with compassion, accuracy, and professionalism during some of their most difficult times.

Vision:To become the most trusted and efficient contents restoration logistics partner in the region.

2. Company Description
The Pack Out King offers a complete solution for the physical handling of home contents during restoration events. When disaster strikes and restoration contractors need space to work, we step in to carefully remove, inventory, and store every item — from clothing and electronics to heirlooms and appliances.

We solve a key logistical and emotional challenge in the restoration process, and we differentiate ourselves with our use of cutting-edge inventory software, responsive crews, and high-standard security protocols.

3. Market Analysis
Industry Overview
	•	The U.S. restoration industry exceeds $210B annually.
	•	Contents handling makes up 10–25% of many restoration claims.
	•	Pack out services are increasingly outsourced for liability, speed, and documentation reasons.

Target Market
	•	Insurance carriers (State Farm, Allstate, Liberty Mutual, USAA etc.)
	•	Third-party administrators (Alacrity, Sedgwick, Contractor Connection)
	•	Local and regional restoration contractors
	•	Direct-to-consumer (disaster-stricken homeowners)

Competitive Landscape
	•	Few pack out specialists focus solely on contents.
	•	Most are extensions of cleaning/restoration firms.
	•	Opportunity exists to brand as a pure-play contents expert.

4. Services Offered
	•	Pack Out Services: Onsite documentation, safe removal, and labeling of contents.
	•	Inventory Management: Digital inventory with photos, condition reports, and barcoding.
	•	Secure Storage: Short- and long-term storage in climate-controlled warehouse.
	•	Pack Back Services: Timely re-delivery and re-staging of property post-repair.
	•	Optional Cleaning Services: Odor removal, textile cleaning, electronics restoration (outsourced or in-house depending on scale).

